.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH thurvtl 1  "thurvtl 0.1.0-dev.4" 
.SH NAME
thurvtl \- ThurVTL Management CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBthurvtl\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
ThurVTL Management CLI
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to configuration file.

Defaults to `/etc/thurvtl/thurvtl.yaml` (thurvtl) or `/etc/thurvsa/thurvsa.yaml` (thurvsa).
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
User to drop privileges to under sudo.

Only applied by daemon\-down commands that write under `data_dir`. Under plain `sudo` those files would otherwise be owned by root and unreadable by the daemon. No effect when the CLI is already running as a non\-root user. Defaults to `thurvtl` (thurvtl) or `thurvsa` (thurvsa).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
thurvtl\-library(1)
Library management (init, info, modify, monitor)
.TP
thurvtl\-cartridge(1)
Cartridge management operations
.TP
thurvtl\-changer(1)
Changer / SMC operations (inventory, move, load, unload)
.TP
thurvtl\-drive(1)
Drive operations and status
.TP
thurvtl\-system(1)
System operations
.TP
thurvtl\-iscsi(1)
iSCSI CHAP credentials
.TP
thurvtl\-config(1)
Configuration helpers (defaults yaml, systemd unit, shell completion)
.TP
thurvtl\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0\-dev.4
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/thurvtl/thurvtl.yaml
Daemon configuration. Minimal starter shipped at install; the
full annotated reference for every key is at
.IR /usr/share/doc/thurvtl/thurvtl.defaults.yaml .
.TP
.I /run/thurvtl/admin.sock
Admin Unix socket the CLI dials for daemon-routed verbs (mode
0660, peer-cred authed).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thurvtld (8)
